# The conda env the launcher builds beside the checkout. 3.6 GB of it, and a
# single `git add -A` in here would stage the lot — this repo was the only one
# of the nine suite tools without a root .gitignore to stop that.
env/
.venv/

# Bytecode caches. Python rewrites these on import, so a committed set goes
# stale the moment anyone RUNS the tool: every checkout then shows a page of
# modified .pyc it never touched, and `bdtools update` refused to move the
# checkout at all ("has local source changes: .../__init__.cpython-310.pyc")
# until the suite was taught to tolerate them in 2026-09. vsnp_gui hit this at
# v0.4.73 and irma_gui on 2026-09-15; nothing is committed here, and this is
# what keeps it that way.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# node_modules and .vite/ are covered by frontend/.gitignore, backend/jobs/ by
# backend/.gitignore.

# macOS Finder metadata. The pipeline is also developed on macOS, and a stray
# .DS_Store in bin/ or database/ would otherwise show as local dirt in every
# checkout.
.DS_Store
